# AI Usage Log – Sprint 1 


--> Task 1.1: Project Structure

Purpose of AI Use: Technical guidance and project planning

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: https://chatgpt.com/share/6aaf19c5-a490-83ea-adfe-3f5100654dff 

AI-Suggested Content: AI provided guidance on the structure for separating the frontend, backend, and database functionality.

Validation: Compared the suggestions with the team's project requirements and the existing project structure.

Decision: Partially accepted (Modified before use). As the suggested technology such as Node.js, Express, JavaScript/HTML/CSS, and MySQL were used, but the use of SQLite as database was rejected. 

Reflection: AI helped clarify how the different technologies would work together and helped establish a suitable starting structure for the project.

Responsible Person: Aminata 



--> Task 1.2 : Design Job Seeker and Employer Registration page 

Purpose of AI Use: Requirements clarification and implementation support 

Chat Link or Prompt/Response:  Same as task 1.1

AI-Suggested Content: AI helped determine how to organize separate registration areas for job seekers and recruiters and suggested the information that should be collected during account creation.

Validation: Compared the suggested fields and account types with the requirements of the recruiting website given by the sprint 1 requirements.

Decision: Modified and accepted. The registration process was implemented for both job seekers and recruiters. (* to note that the html pages layout and css for the registration/ log in are not final as of sprint 1)

Reflection: AI helped identify the information and structure needed for the two different user types. Some suggestions were adjusted to better match the project's requirements.

Responsible Person: Aminata 



--> Task 1.3: Connect the Website to MySQL

Purpose of AI Use: Backend development and database integration

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: Same as task 1.1

AI-Suggested Content:AI provided guidance for installing and starting MySQL, creating the database connection in Node.js, and inserting and retrieving registration information from the database.

Validation:Tested the application locally and verified that newly registered job seeker and recruiter accounts were being stored in MySQL.

Decision: Accepted with modifications where necessary.

Reflection: AI helped explain the connection between the Node.js server and MySQL and helped troubleshoot database-related issues during development.

Responsible Person: Aminata 



--> Task 1.4: Implement Login and Password Security

Purpose of AI Use: Backend implementation and security guidance

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: Same as task 1.1

AI-Suggested Content: AI suggested using Express sessions for maintaining login state and bcrypt for securely hashing user passwords instead of storing passwords as plain text.

Validation: Reviewed the implementation and tested the registration/login functionality locally.

Decision: Accepted and implemented.

Reflection: AI helped introduce basic security practices into the application, particularly password hashing and session management. The implementation was tested to ensure that the login system worked correctly.

Responsible Person: Aminata 


--> Task 1.5: Connecting the profile page and the registraion / log in page 

Purpose of AI Use: Help in merging two projects (profile page and registration/ log in page) 

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: https://chatgpt.com/share/6aaf19c5-a490-83ea-adfe-3f5100654dff 

AI-Suggested Content: AI suggested ways to merge the two projectes together to make a cleaner project. 

Validation: Tested the registration and log in page to verify that it brings the user to the profile page.

Decision: Modified before use.

Reflection: AI helped in making the registration/ log in page linked to the profile page, while giving tips to reduce redundancies in the project. 

Responsible Person: Aminata 



--> Task 1.6: Debug Registration and Server Issues

Purpose of AI Use: Debugging and troubleshooting 

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: In other chats it can be seen where issues arise in each steps. 

AI-Suggested Content: AI analyzed errors encountered while running the Node.js server and displaying/submitting the registration forms. It suggested possible causes and changes to the server and frontend code.

Validation: Applied the suggested changes and tested the application locally to determine whether the errors were resolved.

Decision: Accepted some suggestions and modified others based on the observed results.

Reflection: AI was useful for identifying likely causes of errors and explaining what different error messages meant. However, testing the changes locally was still necessary because some suggestions did not completely solve the problem on the first attempt.

Responsible Person: Aminata 



--> Task 1.7: Configure Git and GitHub based on the VsCode files

Purpose of AI Use: Version control guidance

Chat Link or Prompt/Response: https://chatgpt.com/share/6ab9865e-819c-83ea-af6b-2205b938a8ef 

AI-Suggested Content: AI explained how to add the local VS Code project to the team's existing GitHub repository, how to work with the existing "code" folder, and how to stage, commit, and push changes.

Validation: Checked the Git status and verified that the correct project files appeared in the team's repository.

Decision: Accepted with modifications based on the team's existing repository structure (the repository was already created , therefore only adding the project was needed).

Reflection: AI helped clarify how a local project could be integrated into an existing team repository without unnecessarily adding unrelated files. It also helped explain Git status messages and staged changes using VsCode terminal. 

Responsible Person: Aminata 


End AI Log Sprint 1 _ September 27th 2026 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------




# AI Usage Log – Sprint 2

## --> Task 2.1: Code Verification and Debugging

**Purpose of AI Use:** Technical guidance and debugging assistance.

